each round's test drove a branch that had never run.

Round 29 is the one that changed the COLLECTION rather than the reading: `dsh web` was being SIGKILLed
by the test harness 300 ms into a shutdown that takes ~700 ms, so the process never wrote its coverage
report — and an entire plane of the product (everything reached through the browser) read as untested.

Round 27 corrected the merge rule that produced the middle column: a line was judged by its whole
SPAN, so V8's zero-count range for an untaken sub-expression — `? studio.hostApiVersion()`, starting
62 characters into line 92 — reported as never-executed a line that thirteen processes had executed.
35 of `render-tools.js`'s 89 "dark" lines were false, and the dark list was sending a reader to write
tests for code that runs on every tool call.

Round 28 closed the failure-state half of that file (54 → 33): the block a model reads AFTER a failure
(`incomplete frames:` with each reason, `recovery:` notes, `~unknown remaining`) had never been
